      },
      "message": "fix(bore): a ramp entry descends at the ramp angle, not on a steep chord\n\nA Bore with entry Ramp and no entry ramp angle took the chord from the\nlast ring start to the centre. The chord is one ring radius long, so it\ndescended at up to 84 deg at the cutting feed on a small hole.\n\nThe bore now uses the ring ladder's ramp (#1609): the ramp zig-zags\nalong the radial sweep at the transition's ramp angle. A sweep that is\ntoo short for the ramp gets a plunge at the plunge feed with an entry\nnote. The plunge that starts each ring again after the sweep also gets\nan entry note when the entry is not Plunge.\n\nPinned by bore_ramp_angle (Ø7, Ø12, Ø16, both directions).\n\nFixes #1665\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
